On Mon, Nov 06, 2006 at 01:34:28PM -0500, Matt Arnold wrote:
> My apologies. I have been informed by those who know much more
> about Lojban that Lokadin's orthography is permitted in official
> Lojban. They sent some stuff about "camxes" and "valfendi", which
> are apparently parsers that I've never heard of.

camxes is
http://teddyb.org/~rlpowell/hobbies/lojban/grammar/index.html

Since there's a non-trivial chance it'll become the official parse,
you may want to look at it.

I can't find where valfendi lives these days; it's a morphology-only
parser from the official morphology commision, now semi-defunct.

More relevantly, stress+pauses is the only way to safely transcribe
spoken Lojban; the only real question is how to indicate stress.
Different people have different preferences on this.

Having said all that, it's still amazingly reader-hostile and
obnoxious, and I wish he (Lokadin) would stop doing it.

-Robin

